# Direct dependency intent. The matching .txt beside this file is GENERATED from it (the .txt
# header names the compiler) and must not be hand-edited; scripts/check_requirements_lockfile.py fails CI
# if the two disagree, and the lockfile check runs before anything is installed.
#
# The .txt exists because a transitive dependency cannot be allowed to float between CI
# runs: celery only constrains kombu to <6.0, and kombu 5.7.0's redis extra rejects the
# redis==5.0.4 pinned below, so a fresh resolve on 2026-11-03 turned every branch red
# without a code change. The lockfile pins the whole closure and carries a hash per wheel.
#
# Regenerate (needs the network). Full procedure and the pin-drift gate:
# docs/how-to/recompile-requirements.md
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.14 -o requirements/<name>.txt requirements/<name>.in
# uv is the generator of record: a pip-compile run for this graph wedged on a stalled TLS read
# (0.09s of CPU in 70 minutes). pip-compile still works; the runbook carries its flags.
#
-r base.in

